@@ -57,3 +57,26 @@
 
 Loic Dachary
 loic@gnu.org
+
+Compatibility repairs
+---------------------
+
+The debug callback uses HAS_VSNPRINTF from Perl's config.h, with the
+legacy HAS_VPRINTF check retained for older Perl releases. Perl 5.27.6
+removed HAS_VPRINTF. Check the actual formatting capability in every
+compilation unit instead of defining the obsolete Perl macro globally.
+The matching report and Debian fix are documented at:
+https://rt.cpan.org/Public/Bug/Display.html?id=124815
+https://bugs.debian.org/1075214
+
+All lengths passed through size_t pointers must use size_t storage.
+An int can be smaller than size_t on 64-bit systems, so a cast cannot
+repair the resulting overwrite. This follows the fix credited to
+Hilko Bengen in Debian's patch series for bug 848156:
+https://sources.debian.org/patches/libtext-unaccent-perl/1.08-2/
+
+These changes apply to ordinary Perl and XPerl without version guards.
+Run perl Makefile.PL, make, and make test with the intended interpreter.
+The regression tests cover both conversion entry points, buffer resizing,
+empty input, and conversion with debug output enabled. The library's
+process-global buffers and debug settings do not provide thread isolation.
